WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:03.836
-This week has revealed a lot
about the Trump White House,

00:00:03.836 --> 00:00:07.273
from peddling conspiracy
theories to attacking immigrants

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.575
to defending an aide
accused of domestic violence.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.045
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:16.715
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.715 --> 00:00:19.285
-Donald Trump so badly
wants to be a dictator,

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:22.021
but no one seems
to take him seriously.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.189
Maybe it's his name.

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:26.025
"Donald Trump"
just isn't a good dictator name.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.260
It sounds like the name
of the chubby I.T. nerd

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:30.830
who doesn't get the girl
in a college comedy.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:32.565
"You'll never guess
who asked me out.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.900
Donald Trump."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.970
Still, this week has brought us
one unnerving spectacle

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.805
of authoritarianism
after another,

00:00:39.805 --> 00:00:41.740
from the President
calling Democrats treasonous

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:42.975
for not applauding him

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:45.712
to ordering the Pentagon
to plan a military parade.

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.914
In fact, Trump's request
for a military parade

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:51.351
is so crazy that even
state TV outlet Fox News

00:00:51.351 --> 00:00:53.219
seems a little
uncomfortable with it.

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.355
-Jennifer, what has been
the reaction at the Pentagon

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.790
to the President's request?

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:00.059
-Well, I would describe it,
Dana, as a collective eye roll

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:02.195
from military leaders
who I've spoken to.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.229
Most thought
it was a joke, at first.

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:06.999
Many fear that the U.S.
will look like the dictators

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:08.968
they scoff at around the world.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.403
-There are a lot of people
at the Pentagon

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.906
who would love to show off all
the equipment and personnel.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.941
-I don't know.
It seems like a waste of money.

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:17.877
-Wow!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.745
When you've lost Brian Kilmeade,

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:22.081
you know you've gone off
the deep end.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:23.916
That's like
Thelma telling Louise

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.585
she's just gonna catch an Uber.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.986
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.387
But while they may be skeptical

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.222
of Trump's plan
for a military parade,

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:32.524
Fox News and the rest
of Trump's allies in the GOP

00:01:32.524 --> 00:01:34.960
have been helping him concoct
a series of fake scandals

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.729
to undermine
the Russia investigation,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.565
like, for example,
the famous Nunes memo,

00:01:39.565 --> 00:01:41.234
alleging wrongdoing by the FBI.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.802
The memo turned out
to be a dud,

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.771
but that didn't stop Trump
from pretending

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:46.405
they'd uncovered
a massive scandal

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:48.574
during a speech in Ohio
on Monday.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:50.576
-Oh, but did we catch them
in the act or what?

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:51.610
You know what I'm talk--

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.313
Oh, did we catch them
in the act!

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:56.682
They are very embarrassed.

00:01:56.682 --> 00:01:58.651
They never thought
they would get caught.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.954
We caught them.

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.188
Hey, we caught them.

00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:04.591
Oh, it's so much fun.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:07.159
We're like the great sleuth.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:10.063
-I'm sorry. You are...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.798
You are not a great sleuth.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:12.998
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:15.034
You might think
you're Dick Tracy,

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.103
but you're only half right.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:24.343
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:24.343 --> 00:02:27.213
So, Trump's allies in Congress
and the right-wing media

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.649
have going all out
to discredit the Russia probe,

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.884
and yesterday,
they latched on to yet another

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.020
wild conspiracy theory
when a text message

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.489
from September 2016 emerged

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.225
between former FBI officials
who were having an affair,

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.860
in which one wrote to another...

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:45.131
Now, Fox News tried
to claim the text

00:02:45.131 --> 00:02:46.632
was a reference
to President Obama

00:02:46.632 --> 00:02:48.801
meddling in the Hillary Clinton
e-mail investigation,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:52.004
but if you look at the timeline,
that doesn't make sense.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.140
In fact, it turns out
the text was actually about

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.774
Russian interference
in the election,

00:02:55.774 --> 00:02:57.944
a topic any competent President

00:02:57.944 --> 00:02:59.712
would obviously
want to be briefed on.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.314
Of course,
if that text were sent now,

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.349
under Trump, it would read...

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.887
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:10.222
But as usual, the fact
that this fake scandal

00:03:10.222 --> 00:03:12.324
was yet another dud
did not deter Trump,

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:14.727
who took to Twitter
to scream in all caps...

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.464
This keeps happening.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.132
Every time the right
claims to have discovered

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:21.367
some major bombshell

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.236
casting doubt
on the Russia investigation,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:26.339
we get a little more context,
and it turns out to be B.S.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.540
In fact,
the same guy who brought us

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.142
this fake text scandal,
GOP Senator Ron Johnson,

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:33.079
also brought us a fake
text scandal a few weeks ago

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.847
when he claimed
to have found a reference

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:38.117
to a so-called secret society
in a text message sent

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:40.052
by those same two FBI officials.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:42.921
-What this is all about
is further evidence

00:03:42.921 --> 00:03:46.125
of corruption --
more than bias but corruption --

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.027
at the highest levels
of the FBI.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:50.830
And that secret society,
we have an informant

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.532
that's talking about a group

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:55.234
that were holding
secret meetings off-site.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:58.204
There is so much smoke here,
there is so much suspicion.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:00.072
-Let's stop there.
A secret society,

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.742
secret meetings off-site
of the Justice Department?

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:03.810
-Correct.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.745
-And you have
an informant saying that?

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:06.913
-Yes.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:09.449
-Man, look at Bret Baier's
face right now.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:12.084
That's the face you make
when someone comes up to you

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:14.053
on the subway
and tells you pizza rat

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.555
was a government
mind-control project.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.224
"He didn't want the pizza, man!

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:22.028
They just made him think
he wanted the pizza!"

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:25.731
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:28.000
Now, when the full context
of the message came out,

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.869
it turned out
it was just a joke,

00:04:29.869 --> 00:04:31.904
which anyone with any
common sense could've told you.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.139
And Johnson was eventually
forced to admit

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:36.275
that the whole thing
was probably a joke

00:04:36.275 --> 00:04:38.844
when he was tracked down
by reporters in the Capitol.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:41.814
-Senator,
this text message seems to be --

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.116
the comment about
a secret society was in jest.

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:46.119
Do you agree that it appears
to be it was in jest?

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.221
-Oh, is it?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:52.825
Is it a real possibility,
Detective Johnson?

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.394
I'm sorry to say this,
but you're not exactly a...

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:56.662
-Great sleuth.

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:58.364
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:58.364 --> 00:05:04.837
-Now, while all of this
is happening,

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.805
Special Counsel
Robert Mueller's investigation

00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:10.209
seems to be moving very quickly,
and his team has made clear

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.944
that they would like
to interview Trump soon,

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:13.545
but this week,
Trump's lawyers have been

00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:15.213
telling him not to comply.

00:05:15.213 --> 00:05:18.350
-Lawyers for President Trump
say he should not agree

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.987
to sit down with
Special Counsel Robert Mueller.

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:23.890
That is according
to "The New York Times," saying,

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.891
"Lawyers are concerned
that the President,

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.360
who has a history
of making false statements

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.762
and contradicting himself,

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:32.598
could be charged
with lying to investigators.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:36.602
-Of course, they are.
Trump lies like a rug,

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:39.271
and like his rug,
he's not very good at it.

00:05:39.271 --> 00:05:41.840
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.345
♪ The best thing
that ever happened ♪

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:48.047
-No lawyer
who has ever met Donald Trump

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:50.082
would let him sit down
for an interview under oath

00:05:50.082 --> 00:05:51.316
with Robert Mueller.

00:05:51.316 --> 00:05:53.453
In fact, I'm pretty sure
one of the first questions

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:57.056
on the bar exam is, "Would you
let Trump talk under oath?"

00:05:57.056 --> 00:06:00.359
and the only two choices are,
"No" and "Hell no."

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.562
So you've got the President
ordering military parades,

00:06:02.562 --> 00:06:04.230
calling his political
opponents treasonous

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:05.297
for not applauding him,

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:06.499
and spreading
conspiracy theories

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:07.934
to undermine
a federal investigation.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.536
And then there's the fact that
Trump has been openly lying

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:13.038
about immigration policy,
and just two days ago,

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:15.140
called for a shutdown
of his own government

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.143
if Democrats refused
to bend to his will.

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.544
He was so adamant about it,

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:21.213
he kept repeating the word
"shutdown" over and over.

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:23.348
-If we don't change it,
let's have a shutdown.

00:06:23.348 --> 00:06:27.152
We'll do a shutdown, and it's
worth it for our country.

00:06:27.152 --> 00:06:29.188
I'd love to see a shutdown

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:31.390
if we don't get this stuff
taken care of.

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:33.659
If we have to shut it down
because the Democrats

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:37.863
don't want safety and,
unrelated but still related,

00:06:37.863 --> 00:06:40.199
they don't want
to take care of our military,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.267
then shut it down.

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:44.003
We'll go with another shutdown.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.204
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:46.872
-Why does
he keep saying "shutdown"?

00:06:46.872 --> 00:06:48.640
Is that his safe word

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.577
for when he's confused
and bored in a meeting?

00:06:51.577 --> 00:06:53.412
"Well,
this is all very interesting,

00:06:53.412 --> 00:06:55.581
but I was thinking
we need a shutdown!"

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:56.982
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.982 --> 00:07:00.686
"Let's have a shutdown!"

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:03.255
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:05.224
"Time for a shutdown!"

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:10.562
Also, can we...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:10.562 --> 00:07:12.865
Can we go back
to this part real quick?

00:07:12.865 --> 00:07:15.835
The Democrats
don't want safety and,

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:17.769
unrelated but still related,

00:07:17.769 --> 00:07:20.005
they don't want
to take care of our military,

00:07:20.005 --> 00:07:21.974
-"Unrelated but still related."

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.142
[ Laughter ]

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:25.945
That sounds like
how Trump would describe Eric.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:27.179
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:30.883
"This is, uh...
This is my son."

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:34.454
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:38.223
"This is my son Eric --
unrelated but...

00:07:38.223 --> 00:07:40.827
sadly, related."
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.827 --> 00:07:42.395
Now, leaders in
the Senate yesterday

00:07:42.395 --> 00:07:44.196
reached a deal
to keep the government open,

00:07:44.196 --> 00:07:46.765
but that agreement did not
include a fix for Dreamers,

00:07:46.765 --> 00:07:48.233
the young
undocumented immigrants

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:49.701
who were brought here
as children

00:07:49.701 --> 00:07:51.737
and whose lives
were cruelly thrown into limbo

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.473
when Trump ended the program,
and to protest the fact

00:07:54.473 --> 00:07:56.742
that the deal doesn't include
a solution for dreamers,

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:57.976
Democratic leader Nancy Pelosi

00:07:57.976 --> 00:07:59.445
took to the House
floor yesterday

00:07:59.445 --> 00:08:02.181
and gave an unprecedented
eight-hour floor speech.

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.816
Now, Pelosi has become something
of a target for Trump lately,

00:08:04.816 --> 00:08:06.585
who's been bragging he wants
to make her

00:08:06.585 --> 00:08:09.121
his de facto opponent
during the 2018 midterms.

00:08:09.121 --> 00:08:11.423
Trump even went out of his way
to criticize Pelosi

00:08:11.423 --> 00:08:14.160
during his speech
about the GOP tax cuts in Ohio.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:17.930
-Nancy Pelosi, what
she's doing to this country.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.899
And she's gone so far left.

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:24.736
I think this is not
a good day for Nancy Pelosi.

00:08:24.736 --> 00:08:26.606
She's our secret weapon.

00:08:26.606 --> 00:08:28.541
Your paychecks are going way up.

00:08:28.541 --> 00:08:31.977
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:31.977 --> 00:08:34.680
Your taxes are going way down.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:39.384
So Nancy Pelosi, again,
said that's crumbs.

00:08:39.384 --> 00:08:42.588
Well, she's a rich woman who
lives in a big, beautiful house.

00:08:42.588 --> 00:08:45.658
-So Trump seems to have trained
his sights on Nancy Pelosi.

00:08:45.658 --> 00:08:47.926
I wonder what it is
about Nancy Pelosi

00:08:47.926 --> 00:08:49.528
that seems
to attract Trump's ire.

00:08:49.528 --> 00:08:51.297
I mean,
Trump attacks a lot of people,

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:52.531
but there's something
in particular

00:08:52.531 --> 00:08:53.966
that really seems to anger him.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:56.368
I can't put my finger on it.
It's really a mystery.

00:08:56.368 --> 00:08:58.771
Well, I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:00.839
I guess we'll never know.
We'll just never know.

00:09:00.839 --> 00:09:02.841
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:02.841 --> 00:09:06.278
But there's something.

00:09:06.278 --> 00:09:10.048
In fact, the Trump White House's
misogyny and hostility

00:09:10.048 --> 00:09:12.017
towards women were once again
on display this week

00:09:12.017 --> 00:09:14.286
when administration officials
initially defended

00:09:14.286 --> 00:09:16.388
the White House staff secretary
Rob Porter

00:09:16.388 --> 00:09:19.425
after he was accused by two
ex-wives of domestic abuse.

00:09:19.425 --> 00:09:21.093
It was reported that
senior White House officials

00:09:21.093 --> 00:09:22.961
were aware for months
of the allegations.

00:09:22.961 --> 00:09:25.131
No action was taken
to remove him from the staff,

00:09:25.131 --> 00:09:27.232
and after the allegations
surfaced Tuesday,

00:09:27.232 --> 00:09:28.901
the White House
strongly defended him.

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:30.903
Now, the allegations
against Porter were reported

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:32.171
by two different publications

00:09:32.171 --> 00:09:34.006
and corroborated by photos
and contemporary sources,

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:37.075
but still, the Trump White House
initially defend him.

00:09:37.075 --> 00:09:39.679
In fact, this is a White House
that has repeatedly chosen

00:09:39.679 --> 00:09:42.581
the denials of men over the many
corroborated stories of women,

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.183
whether it's in the case
of Roy Moore,

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:46.252
Corey Lewandowski,
or Trump himself.

00:09:59.531 --> 00:10:01.033 line:0%
-Yeah, we've been clear
on that from the beginning,

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:02.534
and the President's
spoken on it.

00:10:02.534 --> 00:10:04.303
-I can only say
Corey's a fine person.

00:10:04.303 --> 00:10:06.271
I told him, I said you should
never settle this case.

00:10:06.271 --> 00:10:07.640
You should go all the way.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:11.077
I think they've really hurt
a very good person.

00:10:11.077 --> 00:10:13.479
Roy Moore denies it.
That's all I can say.

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:14.613
He denies it.

00:10:14.613 --> 00:10:17.416
And by the way,
he totally denies it!

00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:20.386
-Trump sided with those guys

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:22.154
even though
they look so guilty.

00:10:22.154 --> 00:10:24.155
Roy Moore is what
Howdy Doody would look like

00:10:24.155 --> 00:10:26.459
if he checked in
to a rehab clinic,

00:10:26.459 --> 00:10:28.427
and Corey Lewandowski looks
like he should be

00:10:28.427 --> 00:10:31.263
slowly rising out of a basket
while music plays.

00:10:31.263 --> 00:10:32.698
[ Laughter ]

00:10:32.698 --> 00:10:34.432
Porter resigned yesterday
despite Kelly

00:10:34.432 --> 00:10:36.435
and other White House officials
defending him.

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:38.804
And in the wake
of Porter's resignation,

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:41.173
this photo of a group
of key Trump aides

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:43.442
from a July 2017 event
has resurfaced.

00:10:43.442 --> 00:10:44.810
Look at that photo.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.546
Everyone in that photo has
either resigned or been fired --

00:10:47.546 --> 00:10:50.916
Lewandowski, Omarosa,
Anthony Scaramucci,

00:10:50.916 --> 00:10:53.085
Sebastian Gorka, and Porter.

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:55.554
Even the car in the back
has been fired.

00:10:55.554 --> 00:10:56.922
[ Laughter ]

00:10:56.922 --> 00:11:00.091
Melania kept trying to escape
in it, so it had to go.

00:11:00.091 --> 00:11:01.994
So if you're in the photo,
it means eventually,

00:11:01.994 --> 00:11:03.963
you'll be fired.
And I know it's cheating,

00:11:03.963 --> 00:11:06.264
and I don't know --
maybe this will work?

00:11:06.264 --> 00:11:07.900
There we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:09.201
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:09.201 --> 00:11:12.905
[ Cheers and applause ]

